<section class="shell band faq" id="getting-started">
  <h2>Getting started</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>How do I become a client?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Email the practice to request a free 15-minute consult. If it is a fit, you receive
      client forms and we schedule. If it is not, you get a referral rather than a polite
      brush-off.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Where is Finding Balance Counseling located?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>The practice is based in Austin, Texas, and works online with clients anywhere in the
      state. There is no office clients visit: every in-person session happens outdoors, either on
      a trail in central Texas or with the horses near Dripping Springs. Reem is licensed in
      Texas and sees clients located anywhere in the state online.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Should I see Reem or one of the associates?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Usually it comes down to availability and fee. Reem keeps a small therapy caseload
      alongside her supervision and consultation work, at $240 a session. The LPC Associates she
      supervises have more open calendars and lower fees, including sliding scale, and practice
      under her supervision.</p>
          <p><a href="/therapy/associates/">The associates, with fees and direct contact for each</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Who does Reem work with?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Young adults, college-age clients and individual adults, plus LPC Associates and
      licensed therapists in supervision or consultation. The practice does not work with young
      children.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What are the office hours?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>By appointment. Walk and table therapy sessions are on Fridays.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>

